;; FH-ROOT-003 — two roots of ONE view on one page.
;;
;; The derivation default cannot answer this case alone: both mounts would
;; derive the same id from the same view. So the author states the fact that
;; distinguishes them, in one of two spellings — `:disambiguator`, which
;; APPENDS a scalar to the derived id, or `:root-id`, which names the id
;; outright — and the descriptor records which happened.
;;
;; What must then be true is independence, and independence is proven with
;; state that cannot be shared by accident: each panel's UNCONTROLLED input.
;; Type into the left one and the right one must not move. Two roots sharing
;; a host root, a boundary, or an identity would show it here immediately.
;;
;; The other half of the row is the three admission claims. Each is asserted
;; BEFORE the offending root renders anything, and each leaves the roots
;; already on the page untouched — so the fixture pins both the diagnostic
;; and the fact that the incumbent kept working.
{:fh/id "FH-ROOT-003"
 :fh/law
 "Two roots of one view on one page hold independent identity and independent state — distinguished by :disambiguator or an authored :root-id, each with its own host root, its own occurrence and its own injective identifierPrefix — and the three admission claims (id, container, prefix) each fail loud BEFORE any render, leaving every root already on the page rendering and untouched."

 :view :panel

 ;; The two spellings, and the ids they resolve to.
 :left  {:opts   {:disambiguator :left}
         :root-id [:re-frame.freehand.root-views/panel :left]
         :provenance :derived
         :label  "left"
         :seed   "left-seed"
         :typed  "left-typed"}
 :right {:opts   {:root-id :fh.root/right}
         :root-id :fh.root/right
         :provenance :authored
         :label  "right"
         :seed   "right-seed"
         :typed  "right-typed"}

 ;; An authored id's derived prefix, pinned exactly: the slug is the
 ;; decodable canonical form, so `.` escapes to `_2e_` and the
 ;; namespace/name boundary is the `_S` marker.
 :right-identifier-prefix "rf2-fh_2e_root_Sright-"

 ;; The derived pair need only be DISTINCT — which is the injectivity claim,
 ;; and the reason the framework's own derivation can never trip the
 ;; prefix-uniqueness check.
 :prefixes-distinct true

 ;; The three admission claims. Each names the diagnostic and asserts the
 ;; incumbent root is untouched: still registered, still rendering.
 :claims
 [{:claim :root-id
   :note  "the same root-id, in a DIFFERENT container"
   :error :rf.error/duplicate-root-id}
  {:claim :container
   :note  "a DIFFERENT root-id, into a container another root owns"
   :error :rf.error/root-container-in-use}
  {:claim :identifier-prefix
   :note  "an AUTHORED identifier-prefix that aliases a live root's"
   :error :rf.error/duplicate-identifier-prefix}]

 ;; Nothing is left behind by a rejected mount, because nothing was written:
 ;; the registry still holds exactly the roots that were there.
 :live-roots-after-rejection 2}
